the target language is: lps.

% The same puzzle, stated rather than solved: no decomposition, just denials
% saying when an action is possible, and one goal.
% Source: examples/goat_declarative.pl in the LPS(2) repository.
%
% "the goal is that ..." is the only construct here that the reactive engine
% does not have; it is also the declaration that this is a planning problem,
% so le_lps.pl emits :- lps_engine(planning, ...) alongside it.

the maximum time is 10.

the actions are:
    farmer rows from *a first place* to *a second place*; known as row.
    *an object* is carried from *a first place* to *a second place*; known as transport.

the fluents are:
    *an object* is at *a place*; known as loc.

the knowledge base goat declarative includes:

initially wolf is at south
    and goat is at south
    and cabbage is at south
    and farmer is at south.

when an object is carried from a first place to a second place
then the object is at the second place.

when an object is carried from a first place to a second place
then it is not the case that the object is at the first place.

when farmer rows from a first place to a second place
then farmer is at the second place.

when farmer rows from a first place to a second place
then it is not the case that farmer is at the first place.

it must not be true that
    a first object is carried from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time
    and a second object is carried from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time
    and the first object is different from the second object.

it must not be true that
    farmer rows from south to north from a first time to a second time
    and farmer rows from north to south from the first time to the second time.

it must not be true that
    farmer rows from a first place to a second place to a time
    and goat is at a place at the time
    and wolf is at the place at the time
    and it is not the case that farmer is at the place at the time.

it must not be true that
    farmer rows from a first place to a second place to a time
    and goat is at a place at the time
    and cabbage is at the place at the time
    and it is not the case that farmer is at the place at the time.

% the farmer is not cargo
it must not be true that
    farmer is carried from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time.

% applicability
it must not be true that
    an object is carried from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that farmer is at the first place at the first time.

it must not be true that
    an object is carried from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that farmer rows from the first place to the second place from the first time to the second time.

it must not be true that
    farmer rows from a first place to a second place from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that farmer is at the first place at the first time.

the goal is that wolf is at north
    and goat is at north
    and cabbage is at north
    and farmer is at north.
